  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The Victorian state election has resulted in a significant shift in government, with the Liberal Coalition led by Jess Wilson defeating the incumbent Labor Party. The campaign was marked by intense scrutiny over the Coalition’s economic proposals, which included the privatization of Melbourne's sewage treatment facilities and the sale of state land and renewable energy assets to address government debt and election spending commitments. Labor, led by Ben Carroll, suffered a historic defeat, with Carroll failing to retain his seat in Niddrie, which the party had held for five decades. During the lead-up to the vote, analysts noted the potential for far-right party gains and debated the impact of late-stage policy releases. Western Australian Premier Roger Cook acknowledged the result, noting the distress this outcome causes for his Labor colleagues in the eastern state.",
